---
// Privacy policy for the personal youtube-mcp OAuth app (Google requires a public URL to publish it).
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="youtube-mcp privacy policy" description="Privacy policy for the youtube-mcp tool.">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">youtube-mcp privacy policy</h1>
  <article class="prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert mt-6">
    <p><em>Last updated: October 27, 2026</em></p>
    <p>
      youtube-mcp is a personal tool written and run by naniiluja (Hoàng Minh Quang) on his own computer. It lets
      an AI assistant upload and manage videos on his own YouTube channel through the YouTube Data API. It is not
      offered to the public.
    </p>
    <h2>What data it accesses</h2>
    <p>
      With your consent, the tool uses the <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube</code> scope to read your
      channel details and video list, upload videos, set thumbnails, and edit video titles, descriptions, tags,
      privacy and schedule.
    </p>
    <h2>How data is stored</h2>
    <p>
      The OAuth token is stored only on the local machine running the tool, in a file readable by that user alone.
      Video files are sent directly from that machine to YouTube. No data is sent to any other server, shared
      with third parties, sold, or used for advertising or AI model training.
    </p>
    <h2>Google API Services User Data Policy</h2>
    <p>
      youtube-mcp's use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
      <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Google API Services User Data Policy</a
      >, including the Limited Use requirements. Use of YouTube data is also subject to the
      <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouTube Terms of Service</a>
      and the
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Revoking access and deleting data</h2>
    <p>
      You can revoke access at any time at
      <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >myaccount.google.com/permissions</a
      >. Deleting the local token file removes all stored data.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions: qhm.dev@gmail.com</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
